Monitors the health of the firewall's drives (NVMe, SATA SSD and HDD) using
SMART data from smartmontools.

Adds a "Disk Health" dashboard widget showing, per disk, the overall SMART
verdict, a color coded temperature bar, wear, total data written, bad blocks,
error counters and power-on time. The widget turns red when a disk reports
errors. Collection interval, monitored disks, temperature unit and limits
(globally or per disk) and alerting are configured under Services > Disk
Health; the widget picks which of those disks and which details to show.

Raises a system alert (header status bell) and logs to syslog when a disk is
failing, degrading or too hot.

Requires the os-smart plugin, which is installed automatically.

WWW: https://github.com/priestjim/opnsense-os-diskhealth

